00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:15.849
Ghazi - Zama: And, what we looked at is, you know, we have this FHE technology, how can this be applied to public blockchains? So FHE, for those who don't know, fully homomorphic encryption.

57
00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:24.170
Ghazi - Zama: Is an encryption scheme that allows to manipulate encrypted data without having to decrypt them.

58
00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:31.189
Ghazi - Zama: And full, you know, in the full homomorphic encryption, means that you have a set of operations.

59
00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:44.860
Ghazi - Zama: Usually it's additions and multiplications, but in the case of TFHC, it's pretty much any operation that you can do on integer that is supported in solidity.

60
00:06:45.050 --> 00:07:01.829
Ghazi - Zama: So, Solidity is the coding language for EVMs. You can have additions, multiplications, comparisons, divisions. All this is possible to implement in FHE. So, technically, what it means is that

