00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:09.530
Ghazi - Zama: When you are a validator and you need to execute a smart contract, You can take encrypted inputs.

62
00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:17.139
Ghazi - Zama: You run the smart contract, you get encrypted outputs, you haven't had any exposure to any data.

63
00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:33.159
Ghazi - Zama: You can run a consensus on the encrypted outputs to compare with other validators whether they got the same results that you got, and you put it in the block of the blockchain, in the states of the blockchain.

64
00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:39.769
Ghazi - Zama: And all that without having seen anything. And so that's, you know, how FHE is applied to

